  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "IPv6Layer::parseNextLayer",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/src/IPv6Layer.cpp",
    "description": "When IPv6 next-header is GRE, parseNextLayer() calls GreLayer::getGREVersion(payload, payloadLen) on untrusted payload without validating that payload actually points to a valid in-bounds GRE header for the current packet buffer. In this PoV, this leads to getGREVersion reading from an out-of-bounds location (heap-buffer-overflow at GreLayer.cpp:28). Root cause is missing/insufficient length/bounds validation before GRE version probing in IPv6Layer::parseNextLayer (crash manifests in GreLayer::getGREVersion).",
    "conditions": "FuzzTarget writes attacker-controlled bytes to a temporary pcap/pcapng, reads packets, then constructs pcpp::Packet and recursively parses layers. A packet must be parsed as IPv6 with nextHeader=GRE while the computed payload pointer/length is inconsistent with actual backing allocation (e.g., malformed capture/layer lengths), so GRE probing is attempted on invalid memory. Trigger requires reaching IPv6Layer::parseNextLayer GRE case and invoking GreLayer::getGREVersion on that malformed payload."
  },
